   "source": [
    "# Bias & Fairness Audit\n",
    "\n",
    "Audit face recognition performance across demographic subgroups.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Subgroups Required (AGENTS.md Section 8)\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dimension | Subgroups |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Age | 18–35, 36–60, 60+ |\n",
    "| Gender | M, F, non-binary |\n",
    "| Ethnicity | ≥ 4 subgroups |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "For each subgroup, report:\n",
    "- **FAR** (False Acceptance Rate) — target ≤ 0.1%\n",
    "- **FRR** (False Rejection Rate)\n",
    - **EER** (Equal Error Rate)\n",
    "- **Match rate** — percentage of queries returning a match\n",
    "\n",
    "## Statistical Significance\n",
    "\n",
    "Per AGENTS.md, subgroup-specific thresholds (`T_group`) are allowed\n",
    "**only** if the audit demonstrates a statistically significant disparity\n",
    "(p < 0.05) for a subgroup.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Test\n",
    "\n",
    "Use a chi-squared test or t-test to compare FAR across subgroups:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare FAR between two subgroups\n",
    "chi2, p_value = stats.chi2_contingency(contingency_table)\n",
    "# If p_value < 0.05 → significant disparity → consider T_group\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Demographics Schema\n",
    "\n",
    "Demographics are stored as JSONB in `suspect_profiles.demographics`:\n",
    "\n",
    "```json\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"age_band\": \"36-60\",\n",
    "  \"gender\": \"M\",\n",
    "  \"ethnicity\": \"Caucasian\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Reporting\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Run the bias audit notebook before every threshold change\n",
    "2. Attach the notebook output to any PR that modifies `MATCH_THRESHOLD`\n",
    "3. Document findings in the PR description\n",
    "4. Flag any subgroup with p < 0.05 for further investigation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Legal & Ethical Compliance\n",
    "\n",
    "This system must comply with:\n",
    "- **UK DPA 2018** — data protection for biometric data\n",
    "- **Bridges v. South Wales Police** — proportionality of automated face recognition\n",
    "- **EU AI Act** — high-risk AI system requirements\n",
    "- **Human-in-the-loop** — no autonomous action without confirmation\n",
    "\n",
    "TODO: Populate actual audit data after running on real-world dataset."
   ]
